From c7b7809f975b42844bde1c68ddc21feb9601644d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Dudfield?= <renedudfield@microsoft.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:09:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] app: secureStorage: Migrate legacy AKS GitHub tokens

Plugin-scoped storage cannot read the global key used by older AKS
Desktop releases, which would force upgraded users to authenticate again.
Keep the upgrade inside the main-process storage boundary instead of
exposing legacy global storage to renderer plugins.

Allow only the shipped AKS namespace and exact GitHub key to migrate.
Reuse existing ciphertext, prefer a scoped token that already exists,
and check the prospective snapshot against entry and namespace limits.
Decrypt before persisting so unavailable keys or failed writes leave the
original file recoverable. Retire the legacy copy on save and delete as
well, preventing sign-out from reviving an older token.

This is the narrow compatibility mapping carried as patch 0101 by AKS
Desktop. It adds no configurable mapping or renderer capability and does
not depend on the separate cluster pre-open feature.
